            <ArticleTitle>Primary hyperparathyroidism: an uncommon cause of hip pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>272-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/PEC.0000000000000404</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Hip pain is a common complaint in a pediatric emergency department. The causes of hip pain are diverse and generally include traumatic and infectious causes. We report a case of hip pain caused by deep soft tissue infection associated with hypercalcemia and primary hyperparathyroidism. Atypical presentation of primary hyperparathyroidism may result in a delay in diagnosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
